---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import e from '../data/edition.json';
import {link,date,pct,score,number} from '../components/format';
const periods = ['1D','1W','1M','YTD','1Y','5Y'];
const rows = [...e.instruments].sort((a:any,b:any)=>(b.momentum?.portfolio_momentum_score ?? -1) - (a.momentum?.portfolio_momentum_score ?? -1));
---
<Layout title="The tape · Own the Machine" active="data">
  <div class="wrap"><header class="page-head"><div class="eyebrow">The tape / {date(e.issue_date)}</div><h1>Measure<br />the motion.</h1><p>Security returns in the listing’s currency, followed by momentum within this collection. The score describes relative price behaviour. It is not an investment recommendation.</p></header>
  <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Performance table. Scroll horizontally for all periods."><table><caption class="fineprint" style="text-align:left;padding-bottom:16px">{rows.length} instruments · Sorted by portfolio momentum · A dash means insufficient or unverified data</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Instrument / latest close date</th>{periods.map(p=><th scope="col">{p}</th>)}<th scope="col">Momentum / 100</th><th scope="col">Stage 2</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows.map((i:any)=><tr><td><a href={link(`dossiers/${i.id}/`)}><strong>{i.name}</strong><small>{i.symbol} · {i.currency} · {i.metrics.latest_date || 'Unavailable'}</small></a></td>{periods.map(p=><td title={i.metrics.periods[p]?.base_date ? `From ${i.metrics.periods[p].base_date} to ${i.metrics.periods[p].latest_date}. ${i.return_basis}.` : 'No adequate price history'}>{pct(i.metrics.periods[p]?.return)}</td>)}<td class="data-score">{score(i.momentum?.portfolio_momentum_score)}</td><td><span class:list={['status-chip',{pass:i.momentum?.stage2}]}>{i.momentum?.stage2 == null ? 'Unavailable' : i.momentum.stage2 ? '8 / 8 gates' : `${i.momentum.gates_passed ?? 0} / 8 gates`}</span></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <section class="small-section"><h2>The trend, taken apart.</h2><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Momentum components"><table><thead><tr><th>Instrument</th><th>RS / 99</th><th>Below 52W high</th><th>K-ratio</th><th>Positive 5-session periods / 8</th><th>History</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows.map((i:any)=><tr><td><a href={link(`dossiers/${i.id}/`)}>{i.name}</a></td><td>{number(i.momentum?.rs_rating)}</td><td>{i.momentum?.dist_from_high == null ? '—' : pct(-i.momentum.dist_from_high)}</td><td>{number(i.momentum?.k_ratio,2)}</td><td>{i.momentum?.weeks_strengthening ?? '—'}</td><td>{i.market.bar_count} sessions</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p class="fineprint">The positive-period count uses non-overlapping blocks of five trading sessions. It is not a count of rising weekly momentum scores.</p></section>
  <section class="small-section"><div class="method-grid"><div><h2>A score, with context.</h2><p>Four equally weighted percentile ranks combine relative strength, distance from the 52-week high, annual return and trend consistency. The comparison group is this collection of instruments with sufficient valid history.</p><p>Stage 2 is a separate set of eight trend conditions. Every holding can receive a momentum score, including those outside Stage 2.</p><a class="text-link" href={link('receipts/')}>Read the calculation method →</a></div><div><h2>What changed?</h2>{e.score_changes?.length ? <ul>{e.score_changes.map((s:any)=><li>{s.name}: {score(s.previous_score)} → {score(s.current_score)}</li>)}</ul> : <p>This is the first archived edition. Comparable weekly changes will appear after the next edition is collected.</p>}{e.comparison_universe_changes?.changed && <div class="notice">The comparison universe changed. Score movements may reflect a different peer group.</div>}<p>Short histories remain blank. GE’s long-window data spans changes to its business. See its dossier before interpreting that return.</p></div></div></section></div>
</Layout>
